.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
.TH OCTA-STATUS 1 "" "OCTA-CAPTURE @PROJECT_VERSION@" "OCTA-CAPTURE Manual"
.SH NAME
octa\-status \- read kernel-owned clock status
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBocta-status\fR [ALSA-CARD]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read the read-only ALSA CARD control named OCTA-CAPTURE Status.
Print sample_rate_hz, clock_source, clock_active and raw_status_hex as JSON.
Unmapped status bits remain raw. Clock display activation is not a measurement
of synchronization quality.
.PP
The default ALSA control device is hw:CARD=OCTACAPTURE.
The standalone module must expose the status control.
The read uses the kernel's USB/PM guard and does not detach USB interfaces.

.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success; nonzero indicates a usage, device or operation error.
.SH SEE ALSO
octa-capture(1), octa-status(1), octa-preset(1)
